  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Resilience is the ability of a system to continue operating despite failures. In microservices, failures are expected, not exceptional."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Resilience",
            "definition": "The ability to continue operating despite failures."
          },
          {
            "term": "Failure Isolation",
            "definition": "Containing failures to prevent cascade."
          },
          {
            "term": "Graceful Degradation",
            "definition": "Continuing with reduced functionality."
          },
          {
            "term": "Cascade Failure",
            "definition": "A failure that spreads to other services."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Resilience Principles"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Assume failures will happen",
          "Isolate failures",
          "Degrade gracefully",
          "Recover automatically"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Failure Types"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Network failures: timeouts, connection errors",
          "Service failures: 5xx errors, slow responses",
          "Resource failures: out of memory, thread exhaustion",
          "Dependency failures: database, cache down"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Resilience Patterns"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Pattern", "Purpose"],
        "rows": [
          ["Circuit Breaker", "Stop calling failing services"],
          ["Retry", "Retry transient failures"],
          ["Bulkhead", "Isolate resources"],
          ["Timeout", "Limit wait time"],
          ["Fallback", "Provide alternative response"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Design for Failure"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Microservices must be designed for failure. Every network call can fail. Every service can be slow or unavailable. Resilience patterns handle these failures gracefully."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
